# Text that blinks: SGR 5's slow blink and SGR 6's rapid blink, drawn by
# vtium (vtium/vtium#37). SGR 6 changes phase every 200 ms, 150 times a
# minute, the slowest rate ECMA-48 allows for it. Tier 2 pictures show
# one phase at a time, so this guide shows the blinking itself. The last
# step shows the cursor's blink interval, which a program sets with the
# Linux console's CSI 16 ; n ] (vtium/vtium#404).
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=blink

title: slow blink, rapid blink and the cursor's pace

step: Slow and rapid blink side by side
run: clear; printf '\033[5mslow\033[0m  \033[6mrapid\033[0m  \033[5;6mboth\033[0m  steady\n'; guide-wait
expect: "slow" blinks at vtium's usual pace. "rapid" blinks *clearly faster*,
expect: about two and a half times a second. "both" blinks at the rapid
expect: pace, with "rapid". "steady" *never blinks*.

step: Rapid blink with colors and other attributes
run: clear; printf '\033[6;31;4mred underlined\033[0m \033[6;7mreversed\033[0m \033[6;1mbold\033[0m \033[6m中文\033[0m\n'; guide-wait
expect: each of the four words blinks at the rapid pace. The red word keeps
expect: *its underline* while its letters are hidden, and "reversed" keeps its
expect: light background. Both wide characters *blink together*.

step: Rapid blink stops with the text
run: clear; printf '\033[6mrapid until you press a key\033[0m\n'; guide-wait "Press a key or click to clear the screen."; clear; echo "the rapid text is gone"; guide-wait
expect: the line blinks rapidly until you press a key, then *the screen clears* and
expect: shows "the rapid text is gone", which *never blinks*.

step: The cursor blinks at the pace a program sets
run: clear; printf '\033[16;250]\033[5mslow\033[0m  fast cursor: '; guide-wait ''; printf '\033[16]\n\033[5mslow\033[0m  usual cursor: '; guide-wait ''; echo
do: watch the cursor, then press a key or click; watch it again, and press a key or click to end.
expect: the cursor after "fast cursor:" blinks
expect: *twice as fast* as "slow". Press a key or click, and the cursor
expect: moves to the second line, after "usual cursor:", and blinks
expect: *at the same pace* as "slow". Both words "slow" keep the same pace
expect: throughout.
